# Which engine to build for which Hyprland. One line each:
#
#   <Hyprland commit>  <engine commit>  [<folder>]   # what they are
#
# engine/build.sh reads the Hyprland commit from the installed headers and
# refuses to build when it is not listed here. A line is only added after that
# pair has been built and seen working: the engine hooks into Hyprland's
# private drawing code, and a pairing that merely compiles proves nothing.
#
# The engine commit is a commit of this repository: the build script fetches it
# from here. <folder> is where the engine's Makefile is in that commit: "." (or
# nothing) for the commits that came in with the hyprglass history, where the
# engine was the whole tree, and "engine" for a commit made since the engine
# moved into this repository.
